    pr_ref:  # 36a8
    description: "Found by a read-only source-reading session\n(`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_08212026_0237.md`, findings F1/F2),\nverified independently before acting.\n\n**The leak.** `commit-msg` split each trailer into key / whitespace / value,\ntested **only `$val`** against `brand_re`, and reassembled `${key}${ws}${val}`.\nThe scrub removed the half that *implies* a vendor (a hostname in the value)\nand preserved the half that *names* one.\n\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ABC\n    ^^^^^^ key: untouched          ^^^^^^ value: replaced with an absurd phrase\n\n**Volume, and it was accruing.** Exactly one distinct trailer key in the whole\nhistory matches `brand_re` — `Claude-Session` — on **13** commits. The journal\nmeasured 11; two more landed during the session that measured it, because the\nharness appends that trailer to every agent commit. This was not a static set of\nhistorical commits, it grew by one per commit until fixed.\n\n**Second finding: the body sweep deletes whole lines with no marker**, and the\npattern list contains ordinary English words (Nova, Titan, Granite, Arctic,\nFalcon, Phi, Aya, GLM). The journal called the historical false-positive rate\nunmeasurable, which is correct and I could not break it — git notes restore\nbodies from commits that already passed the hook, and \"zero brand words in\ncurrent bodies\" is circular because a deleted line looks like an absent one.\n\nBut the *prospective* rate is measurable, and it is not hypothetical:\n`falcon` is a web framework **this project supports** (it ships `falcon.yaml`\nand lists it beside django/flask/fastapi). Measured live against the shipped\nhook:\n\n    BEFORE  feat(routes): detect falcon resource classes\n            The falcon analyzer now maps add_route() to its responder methods.\n    AFTER   feat(routes): detect a meerkat djing in a Bronto-burger grill shack\n                          with a panel of dogs resource classes\n            [body line silently deleted]\n\nBoth halves of an ordinary commit damaged: the subject mangled into nonsense,\nthe body line gone with nothing left behind.\n\n## Owner ruling (2026-08-21 interview), recorded verbatim in substance\n\n1. A brand in the **key** replaces the key with `Racial-Capitalism-Is-Bad:`\n   **and forces the value** through the absurd-phrase rewriter *\"even if the\n   value does not contain obvious vendor content\"*. This resolves the journal's\n   open decision 1 in the affirmative: a vendor-named key means the whole\n   trailer is vendor provenance, and a scrubbed key over an intact value would\n   still publish the session id it points at.\n2. On false positives: *\"(a) they make life interesting, and (b) I suppose we\n   could limit the scan to only, e.g., the first 10 lines of the text and the\n   last 10 lines of the text.\"* So the redaction-marker option the journal\n   proposed was NOT taken; the window was.\n\n## What shipped\n\n* Trailer keys are tested, with a three-key allowlist (`Signed-off-by`,\n  `Co-authored-by`, `Co-committed-by`) that is never renamed because\n  `git interpret-trailers`, `%(trailers:key=…)` and DCO validation all key off\n  the exact token.\n* The body sweep is bounded to `body_scan_window` (default 10, env-overridable)\n  lines at each end of the body. Subject and trailers are scanned\n  unconditionally by their own passes — the window narrows only the body.\n\n## Properties verified by execution, not by reading\n\n| property | result |\n|---|---|\n| branded key + branded value | both replaced |\n| branded key + **clean** value | both replaced (ruling 1) |\n| `Signed-off-by` | verbatim |\n| `Co-Authored-By` (capitalised) | key kept, value scrubbed — the `nocasematch` case |\n| idempotent under `--amend` | stable across 3 passes |\n| `Racial-Capitalism-Is-Bad` vs `brand_re` | no collision with any pattern |\n| window discriminates | middle survives, both ends deleted |\n| window control (wide) | all three deleted — non-vacuity floor |\n\n## Deliberately not done\n\n* **Forward-only.** The 13 existing commits keep the leak. Removing it needs a\n  history rewrite and `AGENTS.md` prohibits force-push.\n* **A long body now has an unscanned middle.** That is a coverage-for-precision\n  trade the owner chose knowingly; vendor self-attribution clusters at the\n  subject and the trailers, which are still scanned unconditionally.\n* **No redaction marker.** The journal proposed `[line redacted]` to make body\n  deletions auditable. The owner took the window instead, so a deletion inside\n  the window is still silent."  # 36a8
    fields:  # 36a8
      statement: "A commit message published from this repo must not carry a vendor brand in any position -- subject, body, trailer value, or trailer KEY."  # 36a8
      root_cause: "The trailer loop captured key/ws/value but tested only $val against brand_re, then reassembled ${key}${ws}${val}, so a brand in the key was immune to the scrub by construction. Separately the body sweep deleted whole lines with no marker across the entire body, and the pattern list contains ordinary English words that collide with framework names this project supports (falcon)."  # 36a8
