  message: "CLOSED. Shipped dbf534448c. Behavioral evidence on the MERGED tree, by executing the hook -- a shell rewrite is only knowable by running it.\n\nLIVE REPRO, merged dev, branded key over a CLEAN value (the case the owner ruled on):\n\n  IN   Claude-Session: 12345-plain-identifier\n  OUT  Racial-Capitalism-Is-Bad: a chameleon racing a pie-thrower on the moon\n\nBoth halves replaced, with no brand anywhere in the value that could have triggered the old value-only path. That is ruling 1 working.\n\nTHE WINDOW, with its control. A falcon mention at body line 14 of a 24-line body SURVIVES; the same word inside the window is still DELETED. Both arms run, so this is not a sweep that quietly stopped deleting -- the control took. Suite on the merged tree: 42 passed, 0 failed.\n\nSELF-DEMONSTRATION: the fix scrubbed its own commit. f841d9c2d1 (pre-rebase) carries \"Racial-Capitalism-Is-Bad: a pumpkin-headed crow driving a subway car with a conclave of bats made of bagel chips\" where every prior agent commit carried \"Claude-Session:\". First commit in this history where the KEY is scrubbed rather than only the value.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX, stated so nobody reads the closure as broader than it is:\n1. FORWARD-ONLY. The 13 existing commits keep the leak. Removing it needs a history rewrite and AGENTS.md prohibits force-push.\n2. A LONG BODY NOW HAS AN UNSCANNED MIDDLE. Deliberate, owner-chosen: vendor self-attribution clusters at the subject and the trailers, both still scanned unconditionally, while the middle of a long body is ordinary technical prose. It is a coverage-for-precision trade and the coverage half is real.\n3. DELETIONS INSIDE THE WINDOW ARE STILL SILENT. The source journal proposed a [line redacted] marker to make the body policy auditable; the owner took the window instead. So the falcon class is BOUNDED, not eliminated -- a mention in the first or last 10 lines still vanishes with nothing left behind, and its false-positive rate inside the window remains unmeasurable for the reason the journal gave (the evidence is what the policy destroys).\n4. PYTHON-SIDE NOTHING. This is entirely a git-hook change; no analyzer, no schema.\n\nMETHOD NOTE for whoever audits this next: two of my own test fixtures were wrong before they were right, and both failed in ways that LOOKED like product defects. Fixtures without Signed-off-by tripped the DCO guard and reported as \"CRASH: hook exited with error\" -- the unmodified hook did the same, so it was the fixture. And a window of 1 scanned only the blank separator at body index 0, because the window counts body lines as they are, blanks included; the shipped default of 10 therefore covers 9 lines of real prose at the top. Both are documented in the test file rather than papered over."  # e2c6
